# interplay_fifo_compute_join: A diamond of add_one kernels over four FIFOs: the root computes A = S + 1; child 2 C = A + 1 (gated on the root); child 1 B = C + 1 (gated on child 2); child 3 runs D = B + 1 and E = C + 1 behind two barriers, on child 2 and then child 1, so it passes the first as child 2 publishes and blocks again on the second until child 1 does. Written child 3, child 1, child 2, root; released root, child 2, child 1, child 3. D = S + 4 and E = S + 3 prove every read came after its writer.
